# Undefined macros in AES due to missing includes

- Source URL: https://github.com/chipsalliance/caliptra-rtl/issues/977

On the 2.1 SS FPGA I hack aes_clp_wrapper.sv to include caliptra_reg_field_defines.svh and kv_macros.svh to avoid undefined macro errors. kv_macros.svh gets included from several of the crypto components like ecc, hmac, and sha512 but not for aes. caliptra_reg_field_defines.svh is included mostly from testbenches and soc_ifc.
The workaround for kv_macros.svh is also being used in the 2.0 FPGA.
My ask is that we consider if these includes should be added to AES.

Error requiring caliptra_reg_field_defines.svh:
```
ERROR: [Synth 8-10157] use of undefined macro 'AES_REG_DATA_IN_0' [/fourtb/jlmahowa/caliptra-mcu-sw-lock/hw/fpga/caliptra_build/caliptra_fpga_project.gen/sources_1/bd/caliptra_fpga_project_bd/ipshared/25c5/src/aes_clp_wrapper.sv:190]
```
